X-SOURCE-ID:sabew
X-SOURCE:Sabew
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260529T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260529T140000
DTSTAMP:20260526T230709
CREATED:20260521T174254Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260526T203014Z
UID:71293-1780059600-1780063200@sabew.org
SUMMARY:AI in medical devices: Hype or cost savings? webinar
DESCRIPTION:One of the fastest-growing businesses is integrating AI into all of our medical devices\, from those watch apps to ultrasound machines and medical charts.  How can we get beyond the hype to see what works and what’s bunk? And how can we see if our local hospitals are buying dreams or real patient care? \nThis webinar is in partnership with The National Institute for Health Care Management (NIHCM) Foundation. \nPanelists: \n\nDanny Al-Faruque\, senior editor\, Regulatory Focus\nKatie Palmer\, health tech reporter\, STAT\n\nModerator: \n\nMarty Steffens\, University of Missouri and SABEW chair for business and financial Journalism\n\nRegistration: \nThis is a free webinar\, but you must register below to receive the Zoom link. The link will be sent to all registrants before the event.
URL:https://sabew.org/event/ai-in-medical-devices-hype-or-cost-savings-webinar/
CATEGORIES:Virtual Training
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://sabew.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/May-2026-NIHCM-Webinar-Graphic.jpg
END:VEVENT
